Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:11:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] boards: adapt cv1800b_sophpi_duo_sd for RNSBox (Milk-V
 Duo 64M)

CV1800B (phobos) board dir for the universal CVITEK RV64 image, on the
stock Sophgo/Milk-V Duo 64M SD board:

- memmap.py: headless reclamation - FreeRTOS 768 KB and ION 26.8 MB set
  to 0, handing the whole 64 MB DRAM to Linux (stock handed out ~42%)
- top defconfig: RNSBox shape - sensor blobs dropped, no fb/tp, single
  DTB boot image, the family AIC8800 osdrv recipe kept (dormant here,
  the 64M Duo has no WiFi device); stock KERNEL_LZMA + SKIP_RAMDISK
- kernel defconfig: derived line-for-line from the family RNSBox SG200X
  config; only the chip selection differs (ARCH_CV180X/phobos - the
  CV180X-vs-CV181X choice is a hard Kconfig choice, so phobos and mars
  need one Image each); swap enabled for the 64MB RSS-escape hatch
- u-boot: stock CV1800B SD config, BOOTDELAY=0
- partition xml: RNSBox lite layout (BOOT + ROOTFS), DATA partition and
  the release/usb-flavor extras dropped like every other RNSBox board
